  "text": "HasColumnName the value of \\( A + B + C \\).\n.debugLine\n.debugLine The expression we need to simplify is:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{4} + \\sqrt[3]{8}}{\\sqrt[3]{9} - \\sqrt[3]{6}}\n\\]\n\nFirst, we note that \\(\\sqrt[3]{8} = 2\\), so the expression becomes:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{4} + 2}{\\sqrt[3]{9} - \\sqrt[3]{6}}\n\\]\n\nNext, we want to rationalize the denominator. To do this, we multiply both the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator, which is \\(\\sqrt[3]{9} + \\sqrt[3]{6}\\). This gives:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{4} + 2}{\\sqrt[3]{9} - \\sqrt[3]{6}} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt[3]{9} + \\sqrt[3]{6}}{\\sqrt[3]{9} + \\sqrt[3]{6}} = \\frac{(\\sqrt[3]{4} + 2)(\\sqrt[3]{9} + \\sqrt[3]{6})}{(\\sqrt[3]{9})^2 - (\\sqrt[3]{6})^2}\n\\]\n\nSimplifying the denominator, we get:\n\n\\[\n(\\sqrt[3]{9})^2 - (\\sqrt[3]{6})^2 = \\sqrt[3]{81} - \\sqrt[3]{36} = 3\\sqrt[3]{3} - 2\\sqrt[3]{3} = \\sqrt[3]{3}\n\\]\n\nNow the expression becomes:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{(\\sqrt[3]{4} + 2)(\\sqrt[3]{9} + \\sqrt[3]{6})}{\\sqrt[3]{3}}\n\\]\n\nExpanding the numerator, we have:\n\n\\[\n(\\sqrt[3]{4} + 2)(\\sqrt[3]{9} + \\sqrt[3]{6}) = \\sqrt[3]{4} \\cdot \\sqrt[3]{9} + \\sqrt[3]{4} \\cdot \\sqrt[3]{6} + 2 \\cdot \\sqrt[3]{9} + 2 \\cdot \\sqrt[3]{6} = \\sqrt[3]{36} + \\sqrt[3]{24} + 2 \\cdot \\sqrt[3]{9} + 2 \\cdot \\sqrt[3]{6}\n\\]\n\nSo the expression simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{36} + \\sqrt[3]{24} + 2 \\cdot \\sqrt[3]{9} + 2 \\cdot \\sqrt[3]{6}}{\\sqrt[3]{3}}\n\\]\n\nWe see that the numerator can be rewritten as:\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt[3]{36} + 2 \\cdot \\sqrt[3]{6} + \\sqrt[3]{24} + 2 \\cdot \\sqrt[3]{9} = \\sqrt[3]{36} + 2 \\cdot \\sqrt[3]{6} + \\sqrt[3]{8} \\cdot \\sqrt[3]{3} + 2 \\cdot \\sqrt[3]{9} = \\sqrt[3]{36} + 2 \\cdot \\sqrt[3]{6} + 2 + 2 \\cdot \\sqrt[3]{9} + 2 \\cdot \\sqrt[3]{9} = \\sqrt[3]{36} + 2 \\cdot \\sqrt[3]{6} + \\sqrt[3]{36} + 2 \\cdot \\sqrt[3]{6} = \\sqrt[3]{36} + 2 \\cdot \\sqrt[3]{9}\n\\]\n\nSo the expression becomes:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{36} + 2 \\cdot \\sqrt[3]{9} + 2 \\cdot \\sqrt[3]{6} + \\sqrt[3]{24}}{\\sqrt[3]{3}} = \\frac{\\sqrt[3]{36} + 2 \\cdot \\sqrt[3]{6}}{\\sqrt[3]{3}} = \\sqrt[3]{12} + 2\\sqrt[3]{2}\n\\]\n\nSo the simplified form is:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{3}} \\left( \\sqrt[3]{12} + 2\\sqrt[3]{2} \\right) = \\frac{\\sqrt[3]{12} + 2\\sqrt[3]{2}}{\\sqrt[3]{3}}\n\\]\n\nThus, the values are \\(A = 12\\), \\(B = 2\\), and \\(C = 3\\), so \\(A + B + C = 12 + 2 + 3 = 17\\).\n\nThe final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{17}\n\\]",
